  "notes": "Slice of the fifteen-term decomposition of |T>^10 (S. Bevins, arXiv:2610.17500, filed as qubit_T-m10-upper-15.json): applying (I (x) <0|) to the last qubit on both sides gives <0|T> |T>^9 as a combination of the fifteen projected terms, each a nine-qubit stabilizer state, all nonzero and distinct. Each coefficient is Bevins' coefficient times the scalar by which the projected term differs from the stabilizer state written here, divided by <0|T> = sqrt((3 + sqrt 3)/6); every step is exact and nothing is fitted. chi(|T>^9) <= 15 gives exponent 0.4341 against the m=10 record 0.3907 and the product bound 18 (m=4 times m=5). It fills a cell that had no bound and moves no exponent; the lower bound of the same cell is 6 by projection monotonicity."
